+# Mobile document checklists and named uploads
+
+Phase 10 follows backend 42b4552 with the six preceding mobile patches (v4, claims, notifications, SMS, biometrics, support). Apply mobile-document-requirements.patch last. No migration, dependency or staff frontend change is needed.
+
+GET /api/v1/mobile/beneficiaries/me/document-requirements requires a mobile session. It accepts page (default 1) and pageSize (default 10, maximum 20), and returns programs plus pagination. A program contains only id, code, name, status and requirements. Each requirement contains docType and nullable documentName. All ACTIVE program checklists are readable for preparation; CLOSED programs appear only if the signed-in beneficiary has an enrollment in them. DRAFT/CANCELLED programs and other people's closed-program enrollments are excluded. Viewing a checklist does not submit an application, evaluate criteria or approve eligibility. Staff fields, budget, criteria and enrollment records are not returned.
+
+Other requirements expand otherRequiredDocumentNames into separate entries, with the older singular name as fallback. These are the same strings used by staff enrollment validation. Documents remain beneficiary-level records reusable across programs; there is no new document-to-program approval or invented requirement ID.
+
+Mobile document metadata now includes nullable documentName. Existing multipart uploads accept that field through the shared metadata validator. Mobile sends a trimmed name for OTHER and all eight supported types are selectable. Identical bytes under different named requirements remain distinct; exact retries retain the existing record. Receiving a named file still requires staff review and does not approve enrollment.
+
+An OTHER correction retains its original documentName, including its canonical spelling. A supplied equivalent name is compared after trimming/case/whitespace normalization; a different name returns DOCUMENT_NAME_MISMATCH. A named correction cannot repurpose a previously unnamed record. Omitting the name preserves legacy correction behavior. Existing owner checks, review transitions, replacement replay, private file storage and failed-upload cleanup remain in effect.
+
+Verification: run mobile npm.cmd run test:shared sequentially against isolated migrated PostgreSQL 51244. The actual client/API suite checks program visibility/privacy/pagination/auth, distinct same-content named uploads, retries, rejection/correction with canonical name retention, cross-owner rejection, staff visibility and successful enrollment approval only after both named documents and the birth certificate are accepted. Mobile regressions cover web/native multipart names, validation, EN/BS failed input, immutable correction names and stale checklist responses. No live beneficiary records are changed by these synthetic tests.
